conductor-sync for Fedora and Basalt OS
=======================================

Installing the package creates the "conductor-sync" system user
(sysusers.d), /etc/conductor-sync (root:conductor-sync 0750) with
credentials/ (conductor-sync 0700), the configuration file
/etc/conductor-sync/conductor-sync.toml (mode = "dry-run", 0640) and
/var/lib/conductor-sync. It does not enable or start anything. Where the
targeted SELinux policy is installed, conductor-sync-selinux comes with it
and the service runs in conductor_sync_t.

  1. A read-only AD account; its password in credentials/ad-bind and a state
     key in credentials/state-key (both 0600, owned by conductor-sync).
  2. The domain CA in /etc/conductor-sync/domain-ca.pem; edit
     conductor-sync.toml.
  3. With conductor's "Google Workspace sync" section:
       sudo systemctl enable --now conductor-sync-api.socket
     (the socket's group is "conductor": install conductor first).
  4. Scheduled runs, after a first manual apply:
       sudo systemctl enable --now conductor-sync.timer

Upgrades restart the management API when it is running. "dnf remove
conductor-sync" stops and disables the units and removes the packaged
files; it keeps the credentials (state key), /var/lib/conductor-sync
(links, runs, audit log) and the system user.

Full guide: https://github.com/openbasalt/samba-conductor-sync/blob/main/docs/install-fedora.md
